WEBVTT

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:14.400
Listen!

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.375
After all, if the stars are lit —

00:00:16.375 --> 00:00:18.455
Does that mean — somebody needs them?

00:00:18.455 --> 00:00:20.535
Does that mean — somebody wants them to be?

00:00:20.535 --> 00:00:22.455
Does that mean — somebody calls these little specks of spit

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:23.575
A pearl?

00:00:23.575 --> 00:00:24.375
And, straining himself to breaking,

00:00:24.375 --> 00:00:25.975
In blizzards of midday dust,

00:00:25.975 --> 00:00:26.935
He bursts in on God,

00:00:26.935 --> 00:00:28.135
Afraid he’s come too late,

00:00:28.135 --> 00:00:28.695
Weeps,

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:30.400
Kisses His sinewy hand,

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:30.960
Begs —

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:32.640
That there must be a star! —

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:33.200
Swears —

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.360
He won’t survive this starless torment!

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:36.080
And afterward

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:37.120
He goes about anxious,

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:38.240
But calm on the outside.

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:39.040
He says to someone:

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:40.240
“You’re all right now, aren’t you?

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:41.680
Not afraid?

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:44.175
Yes?!”

00:00:44.175 --> 00:00:45.775
Listen!

00:00:45.775 --> 00:00:46.815
After all, if the stars

00:00:46.815 --> 00:00:47.775
Are lit —

00:00:47.775 --> 00:00:49.855
Does that mean — somebody needs them?

00:00:49.855 --> 00:00:51.135
Does that mean — it is essential

00:00:51.135 --> 00:00:52.015
That every evening

00:00:52.015 --> 00:00:52.655
Above the rooftops

00:00:52.655 --> 00:00:57.115
At least one star should light up?!
